Package: dcsbm
Title: Bayesian Weighted Degree-Corrected Stochastic Block Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Holland", "Whitworth", email = "hwhitworth516@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits a Gaussian degree-corrected stochastic block model to a
    weighted network via Gibbs sampling, with an optional localized
    edge-covariate effect (a continuous covariate and/or a binary edge
    indicator, each with its own block-pair-specific coefficient) and an
    optional "reallocate" Metropolis-Hastings move that jointly redistributes
    node memberships between two existing blocks to improve within-chain
    mixing. K (the number of blocks) is fixed and user-specified; see
    select_K() for a helper that sweeps a grid of K values.
